<title>AUSTRIA: Radex 1996 group net profit up 24 pct.</title>
<headline>Radex 1996 group net profit up 24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary results for the business year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of schillings unless stated)</p>
<p>					 1996		1995</p>
<p> Group sales		     21,007     vs   21,691</p>
<p> Group pre-tax			674     vs	577</p>
<p> Group net			    580     vs	467</p>
<p> Group EPS (schillings)	    36     vs	 30</p>
<p>Fireproof/engineering divison:</p>
<p> Total sales		     16,679     vs   17,477</p>
<p>    Fireproof		    14,829     vs   15,219</p>
<p>    Engineering		   1,850     vs    2,258</p>
<p> Total pre-tax			581     vs	483</p>
<p>    Fireproof			 628     vs	542</p>
<p>    Engineering		     -47     vs	-59</p>
<p>Insulation division:</p>
<p> Sales				4,366     vs    4,252</p>
<p> Pre-tax				138     vs	162</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name is Radex-Heraklith Industriebeteiligungs AG. Radex own 51 percent of Germany's Didier-Werke AG. Analysts had been looking for a group net profit of around 470 million schillings.</p>
</text>
